  - climate justice
  - systems thinking
  - climate science
  - sustainability
abstract: |
  Probatio Systemica provides a neutral mathematical framework for systematic
  verification of complex decisions, formalized through the SEC-J principle
  (Sufficient, Efficient, Consistent, Just) with J-veto at J < 0.50.
  Provolution applies this framework to climate transformation, with the
  Multi-Impact Assessment Framework v2.0 as operational measurement layer
  covering 6 dimensions (GHG, Environmental, Social, Energy, Governance,
  Pathways). Screened technical/systemic potential (not a forecast):
  -58.6 Gt CO₂/year (direct, CO₂-only) across 49 levers in 11 domains
  (A-K) including community-integrated submissions; realistic net
  expectation -43.2 Gt/year (Monte-Carlo median). Authoritative values:
  canon/STATUS.md and canon/data/*.yaml.
